  "kanji": "鳴",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 鳴\ntitle: animal call; ring\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-2, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 14\nradical: 鳥\nradicalNumber: 196\nonyomi: [メイ]\nkunyomi: [な.く, な.る, な.らす]\ndistractors: [鳥, 問, 駅]\n---\n\n# 鳴 — animal call; ring\n\n**Strokes:** 14 · **Key (radical):** 鳥 (no. 196) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n鳴 covers animal calls and other sounding or ringing.\n[鳴く](../words/鳴く.md) なく describes an animal making its call;\n鳴る (なる) describes something such as a bell sounding.\nThe verb ending determines which construction you have.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** [口](口.md) beside [鳥](鳥.md) suggests a bird making a call.\nThis is an explicitly modern memory aid, not a verified explanation of the character's historical formation.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| な.く | kun | [鳴く](../words/鳴く.md) なく — make an animal call |\n| な.る | kun | 鳴る なる — ring; sound |\n| な.らす | kun | 鳴らす ならす — ring or sound something |\n\nThe metadata also records the on reading メイ.\n\n## Common words\n\n- [鳴く](../words/鳴く.md) なく — chirp; meow; bark, according to the animal\n- 鳴る なる — sound; ring\n- 鳴らす ならす — make something ring\n\n## Notes\n\n泣く (なく) means to cry or shed tears; 鳴く does not assert that an animal is weeping.\n鳥 by itself names the animal and lacks the left 口.\n[問](問.md) encloses a 口 instead; [駅](駅.md) has 馬 rather than 鳥 as its large component.\n\nDictionary: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1229840, 1532870, 1532880, 1532910.\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project).\n",
